# 📦 map-gl-offline

An npm package for **Mapbox GL JS** and **MapLibre GL JS** that allows offline storage and usage of vector and raster tiles, sprites, styles, and entire map regions. The package also supports custom layers and region management, including updating, deleting, and handling various zoom levels for offline areas. This package uses the [`idb`](https://www.npmjs.com/package/idb) library for efficient IndexedDB management and supports custom layers and different zoom levels.

---

## 🚀 Features

- 🌐 **Offline Support** for entire map regions
- 🗂️ **Vector & Raster Tiles** Offline storage of vector and raster tiles using idb (IndexedDB).
- 🎨 **Sprites & Styles** Default style handling with support for custom styles.
- 🗂️ **Custom Layers** Add custom layers with ease.
- 🔄 **Region Management:** Download, update, and delete
- 🔍 **Multi-Zoom Level Support**  Handle multiple zoom levels for offline areas.
- ⚡ **IndexedDB Integration**  Fast and efficient storage with IndexedDB. `idb`
- ⏰ **Automatic Expiry Management** Configurable region expiry with automatic cleanup
- 🧹 **Background Cleanup** Automatic removal of expired regions

---

## 📦 Installation

```bash
npm install map-gl-offline
```

> **Note:** This package requires either `mapbox-gl` or `maplibre-gl` as a peer dependency.

```bash
npm install mapbox-gl maplibre-gl
```

---

## 🛠 Usage

### 1. **Import and Initialize**

```typescript
import mapboxgl from 'mapbox-gl';
// or
import maplibregl from 'maplibre-gl';

import { OfflineMapManager } from 'map-gl-offline';

mapboxgl.accessToken = 'YOUR_MAPBOX_ACCESS_TOKEN';

const map = new mapboxgl.Map({
  container: 'map',
  style: 'mapbox://styles/mapbox/streets-v11',
  center: [-74.5, 40],
  zoom: 9,
});

const offlineManager = new OfflineMapManager();

// Optional: Configure custom expiry (default is 30 days)
const customOfflineManager = new OfflineMapManager(1000 * 60 * 60 * 24 * 7); // 7 days
```

### 2. **Add a Region for Offline Use**

```typescript
await offlineManager.addRegion({
  id: 'nyc-region',
  name: 'New York City',
  styleUrl: 'https://api.maptiler.com/maps/streets/style.json',
  bounds: [
    [-74.25909, 40.477399], // Southwest coordinates
    [-73.700272, 40.916178], // Northeast coordinates
  ],
  minZoom: 10,
  maxZoom: 15,
  deleteOnExpiry: true, // Automatically delete when expired (default: false)
});

console.log('NYC region downloaded for offline use!');
```

### 3. **Load an Offline Region**

```typescript
await offlineManager.loadRegion({
  id: 'nyc-region',
  // ... other region options
});
console.log('NYC region loaded from offline storage!');
```

### 4. **Automatic Expiry Management**

```typescript
// Start automatic cleanup (runs every hour by default)
// Only regions with deleteOnExpiry: true will be auto-deleted
const cleanupInterval = offlineManager.startAutoCleanup();

// Manual cleanup of expired regions (respects deleteOnExpiry setting)
const cleanedCount = await offlineManager.cleanupExpiredRegions();
console.log(`Removed ${cleanedCount} expired regions`);

// Force cleanup all expired regions (ignores deleteOnExpiry setting)
const forceCleanedCount = await offlineManager.forceCleanupExpiredRegions();
console.log(`Force removed ${forceCleanedCount} expired regions`);

// Get expired regions breakdown
const expiredRegions = await offlineManager.getExpiredRegions();
console.log(`Auto-deletable: ${expiredRegions.autoDelete.length}`);
console.log(`Manual-only: ${expiredRegions.manualOnly.length}`);

// Check region expiry status
const expiryInfo = await offlineManager.getRegionExpiry('nyc-region');
if (expiryInfo?.expired) {
  await offlineManager.extendRegionExpiry('nyc-region');
  console.log('Region expiry extended');
}

// Stop automatic cleanup when no longer needed
offlineManager.stopAutoCleanup(cleanupInterval);
```

### 5. **List Stored Regions**

```typescript
const regions = await offlineManager.listRegions();
console.log('Stored offline regions:', regions);
```

### 6. **Delete a Region**

```typescript
await offlineManager.deleteRegion('nyc-region');
console.log('NYC region removed from offline storage.');
```

---

## ⚡ API Reference

### `OfflineMapManager`

#### **Constructor**

```typescript
new OfflineMapManager(regionExpiryMs?: number)
```

- `regionExpiryMs` (optional): Region expiry time in milliseconds (default: 30 days)

#### **addRegion(region: OfflineRegionOptions): Promise<void>**

Downloads and stores the specified region offline.

#### **loadRegion(region: OfflineRegionOptions): Promise<void>**

Loads the offline region into the map.

#### **listRegions(): Promise<OfflineRegionOptions[]>**

Lists all regions stored offline.

#### **deleteRegion(regionId: string, styleId?: string): Promise<void>**

Removes the specified region from offline storage.

#### **cleanupExpiredRegions(): Promise<number>**

Removes expired regions that have `deleteOnExpiry: true`. Returns the number of regions cleaned up.

#### **forceCleanupExpiredRegions(): Promise<number>**

Removes all expired regions regardless of the `deleteOnExpiry` setting. Returns the number of regions cleaned up.

#### **getExpiredRegions(): Promise<{autoDelete: StoredRegion[], manualOnly: StoredRegion[]}>**

Gets all expired regions categorized by auto-deletable and manual-only.

#### **startAutoCleanup(intervalMs?: number): ReturnType<typeof setInterval>**

Starts automatic cleanup of expired regions. Default interval is 1 hour.

#### **stopAutoCleanup(intervalId: ReturnType<typeof setInterval>): void**

Stops automatic cleanup.

#### **getRegionExpiry(regionId: string): Promise<{expiry: number, expired: boolean} | null>**

Gets expiry information for a region.

#### **extendRegionExpiry(regionId: string): Promise<void>**

Extends a region's expiry by the default expiry time.

---

## 🔄 Region Options (`OfflineRegionOptions`)

```typescript
interface OfflineRegionOptions {
  id: string;
  name: string;
  styleUrl?: string;
  bounds: [[number, number], [number, number]]; // [[west, south], [east, north]]
  minZoom: number;
  maxZoom: number;
  multipleRegions?: boolean;
  styleId?: string;
  expiry?: number; // Timestamp when region expires
  deleteOnExpiry?: boolean; // Whether to auto-delete when expired (default: false)
}
}
```

